      ":question/problem": "![](images/20/209362c356aa09db8f0c890b833a1aa56cbfbfc6d1ea97e14ea51bd4ca04a47d.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $ABCD$ is a parallelogram.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The point $E$ bisects the diagonals $AC^(\u2015)$ and $BD^(\u2015)$.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $ABCD$ is a parallelogram | Given |\n| 2 | $AB^(\u2015)\u2225CD^(\u2015)$ | Definition of a parallelogram |\n| 3 | $\u2220ABD\u2245\u2220BDC$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 4 | $\u2220BAC\u2245\u2220ACD$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 5 | $AB^(\u2015)\u2245CD^(\u2015)$ | Property of a parallelogram |\n| 6 | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n| 7 | $AE^(\u2015)\u2245EC^(\u2015)$ and $BE^(\u2015)\u2245ED^(\u2015)$ | CPCTC |"
