      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242766",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/46/4646e5edb86a6dbbfaf4b62e7f0fae51bfd0c5ea8d24b5fa7a304692d7cba135.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the diagonals of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ bisect each other.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$ABCD$ is a parallelogram.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $AE^(\u2015)\u2245EC^(\u2015)$ and $BE^(\u2015)\u2245ED^(\u2015)$ | Given |\n| 2 | $\u2220AEB\u2245\u2220CED$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 3 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $\u2220BAE\u2245\u2220ECD$ | CPCTC |\n| 5 | $AB^(\u2015)\u2225CD^(\u2015)$ | Converse alternate interior angles theorem |\n| 6 | $\u2220BEC\u2245\u2220AED$ | Vertical angles theorem |\n| 7 | $\u25b3BEC\u2245\u25b3DEA$ | SAS congruence criterion |\n| 8 | $\u2220EBC\u2245\u2220EDA$ | CPCTC |\n| 9 | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |\n| 10 | $ABCD$ is a parallelogram | Definition of a parallelogram |"
    }
